"last_played": 1371736429, "avatar": "a73955f5d746e6e266b5170c2eed3047928ff0b7"}, "language": "english", "review": "Alien Swarm is a free shooter with a top-down view.  It is a purely cooperative game where a team of four players must clear stages by completing various objectives. The enemies are AI controlled, insect-like aliens. The game supports forty weapons and items, has multiple character and class options and allows creative players to create their own content.\nAlien Swarm uses a simple lobby-based system where players can create or join matches. It is possible to join public channels, or to play alone or with friends.\nPlayers do gain levels, unlock achievements, new equipment and other features as they progress. \nUnfortunately there is only one single official campaign which is composed of seven maps.\nAlien Swarm is a good free game which brings several hours of fun. The fun would last longer if there were more maps available. \nAll in all for fans of cooperative games it is a good choice to try it out. \n\nSounds 7/10\nGraphics 7/10\nGameplay 8/10\nAtmosphere 8/10\n\nIf you liked my review, please feel free to follow me and/or my curator group:\nhttp://steamcommunity.com/id/Ov3RT4K3R/myworkshopfiles/?section=guides\nhttp://steamcommunity.com/groups/orcollective#curation\n\nAlso feel free to check out my YouTube Channel: \nhttps://www.youtube.com/channel/UC83DYCmrWfl9ttrhX54jmWA", "timestamp_created": 1371739944, "timestamp_updated": 1489171266, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 5, "votes_funny": 1, "weighted_vote_score": "0.509090900421142578", "comment_count": 1, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1279569600", "reactions": []}]}